  or federalization or federalism  and that was considered a separatist  statement and therefore he was put under  house arrest so my immediate reaction as  a canadian is to say like what  uh  canada is a federation  not only is canada a federation  but one of the provinces has been ruled  for a good part of the last 35 years by  a separatist government and that the  separatist government on two occasions  has organized a referendum on separation  and while there were detailed rules  about how much advertising for the yes  and the no and stuff like that which our  federal government tried to circumvent  and that created a big scandal  nevertheless uh there have been two  referenda and so the government the  separatist government of quebec  regularly participates in meetings with  the other  provincial premiers in canada so the  word federalist  in a quebec content context means  someone who is pro the central  government and a separatist is someone  who is who wants to separate but he's  still not a criminal  but in ukraine the word federalist is  almost  criminal and the word separatist is like  traitor  so that comes as a bit of a shock  initially  then there was another portion of the  discussion where dobkins said  you know we've lost  crimea we should stop saying we're gonna  get it back because we can't just get it  back  however  what happened there is that those people  decided  to become russian  so if we want them back we have to  persuade those people to want to become  ukrainian again  um  when i hear that i say to myself so  there's an issue here of persuading  people  whether they want to be this or that  that seems to open up  pandora's box in terms of trying to  persuade  citizens of eastern or southern ukraine  to become  russian or ukrainian  in other words if it's a matter of of  constantly trying to persuade people  where they belong  uh that opens opportunities  for  um more referenda  not to mention the fact that quite  obviously in russia you 